#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Normally, the Java environment has been configured after installing the "
"binary version, and can be used with the just built package as well.  Review"
" <xref linkend=\"ojdk-conf\"/> in case you want to modify something."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:528
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test if the man pages are correctly installed, issue <command>source "
"/etc/profile</command> and <command>man java</command> to display the "
"respective man page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:537
#, xml-text
msgid "Setting up the JRE Certificate Authority Certificates (cacerts) file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:541
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have run the instructions on the <xref linkend=\"make-ca\"/> page, "
"you only need to create a symlink in the default location for the "
"<filename>cacerts</filename> file. As user <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:547
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ln -sfv /etc/pki/tls/java/cacerts "
"/opt/jdk/lib/security/cacerts</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:550
#, xml-text
msgid "To check the installation, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:553
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cd /opt/jdk\n"
"bin/keytool -list -cacerts</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/prog/openjdk.xml:557
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"At the prompt <computeroutput>Enter keystore password:</computeroutput>, "
"enter <userinput>changeit</userinput> (the default) or just press the "
"<quote>Enter</quote> key. If the <filename>cacerts</filename> file was "
"installed correctly, you will see a list of the certificates with related "
"information for each one. If not, you need to reinstall them."
msgstr ""

